<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Someshvara III</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 1126–<a href="/years/1138">1138</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Bhulokamalla</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Someshvara III, also called Bhulokamalla, was king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-chalukya-empire">Western Chalukya Empire</a> from 1126 to 1138, the son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikramaditya-vi">Vikramaditya VI</a>. His reign was mostly peaceful, though the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hoysala-empire">Hoysalas</a> and other feudatories grew more independent. A learned king, he compiled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manasollasa">Manasollasa</a>, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanskrit">Sanskrit</a> encyclopaedia of royal life and government completed in 1129.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/someshvara-iii.jpg" alt="Someshvara III" width="320" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dineshkannambadi · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Old_Kannada_inscription_(1129_AD)_at_Kedareshvara_temple_in_Balligavi.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
